WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.260
A Quiet Place is a chilling but riveting film
that delivers a fresh twist on the horror

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:06.260
genre.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:09.640
Yippee ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here
and today I'm breaking down the ending to

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:13.630
A Quiet Place, plus explaining some details
you probably didn't know about the creatures

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:14.630
in the movie.

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:19.150
If this is your first time here, I do regular
movie breakdowns, so if you enjoy this video

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:21.289
be sure to subscribe for more.

00:00:21.289 --> 00:00:26.050
Spoiler warning, I'll be discussing the whole
movie, so take care if you've not seen it

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:27.050
yet.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:31.579
A Quiet Place is set in a near future in which
an alien invasion has decimated swathes of

00:00:31.579 --> 00:00:33.620
the human population around the world.

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:37.910
The creatures have super-sensitive hearing
and so survivors like the Abbotts live as

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:39.170
quietly as possible.

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:43.820
This is why John Krasinski's character Lee
puts down sand trails to muffle sounds while

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:48.620
walking and everyday life has been completely
adapted to dampen any sound.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:52.940
The monsters are blind, so visual signals
are an important way for the human characters

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:54.170
to communicate.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:58.010
And because the family have a deaf daughter,
they have been able to use the American Sign

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:01.300
Language they learned with her to talk silently
with each other.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:07.000
Ok, let's take a look at the alien creatures
and why they attack anything making a sound.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.760
Design-wise the aliens are rather interesting
– they're different from but do bring to

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:15.120
mind other creatures like the Demogorgon in
Stranger Things, the xenomorph in the Alien

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:20.000
movies, the monster in Cloverfield, and the
crazy sharp teeth you see with Venom.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:24.070
The film's production designer Jeffrey Beecroft
has said that he took inspiration for the

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:26.130
alien's form from a Nautilus shell.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:30.930
The nautilus is a type of sea creature that
has very poor eyesight although A Quiet Place

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:34.590
dials that up, making the aliens completely
blind.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:39.250
By the way, there are various newspaper clippings
which describe the aliens as either "Death

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:44.600
Angels" or "Angels of Death" which is interesting
because, in the Jewish tradition, the archangel

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:49.160
Samael is known as the angel of death and
is sometimes referred to as the "blind god"

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:50.160
as well.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:54.860
And the aliens really do seem to be the bringers
of death, but Lee has been researching them

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:58.850
extensively and on his white board we can
see the main things he knows about them.

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:03.040
One thing he's still trying to figure out
is the answer to the question "Why don't they"

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.950
– I think that says – "eat their kill?"

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:09.490
Although the movie doesn't seem to touch on
this in an obvious manner, production designer

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:14.400
Jeffrey Beecroft has explained that "when
loud sound vibrates inside [the aliens' body],

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:18.210
it's intensely painful and they will destroy
anything that makes noise."

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:23.310
And we do see them pulsating and thrashing
around when they're faced with a big sound.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:27.630
Which means the real reason why the creatures
attack anything making a loud noise isn't

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:32.510
for sport or for food – instead, it seems
like they're trying to eliminate [loud] sounds

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:34.220
in the environment around them.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:39.750
And, of course, as the family eventually discovers,
although the aliens' hypersensitivity to sound

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:44.790
makes them deadly to life on earth, it's actually
their weakness as well.

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:48.890
And that makes Lee's efforts to develop a
working hearing aid for his daughter Regan,

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:51.420
played by Millicent Simmonds, the key to the
story.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:55.800
The new hearing aid he gives her doesn't work
properly and creates a high-pitched sound

00:02:55.800 --> 00:03:00.890
that is not only uncomfortable to her, but
is also unbearable to the creatures when they're

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:01.890
nearby.

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:06.010
It seems likely that because the aliens are
blind, they rely on a sort of echolocation,

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:10.410
or bio sonar to emit soundwaves that they
can track to navigate and hunt.

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:14.830
These soundwaves create audio feedback when
they hit the amplifiers in Regan's hearing

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:20.830
aid and, because of the creatures' audio hypersensitivity,
the amplified feedback sound ends up being

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:23.240
extremely painful for the aliens.

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:26.800
Now, when you watched the movie you may have
been hoping that Regan knew this when she

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:31.150
and her brother were hiding in the car as
it could have saved their father, but at that

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:36.350
moment she didn't understand that the hearing
aid's audio feedback was affecting the aliens.

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:40.280
When it happened the first earlier, the alien
was behind her in the corn field and although

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:44.820
we could hear the creature rustling, because
Regan is deaf, she had no idea it was behind

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:45.900
her – all she could feel was the uncomfortable
pitch from the feedback loop right by her

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:46.900
head.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:49.810
And when Regan and her brother were in the
silo, although she also felt the feedback

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:53.590
she didn't realise that was the reason the
creature ran off.

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:57.069
It's not until Regan is in the basement with
her mother and they are confronted with an

00:03:57.069 --> 00:04:02.000
alien that suddenly goes into an uncontrollable
spasm that Regan understands her hearing aid

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.280
has uncovered the monster's weakness.

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:07.030
But the feedback doesn't kill the creature
and it comes back at them.

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:11.900
However, its head is exposed as it opens up
so Evelyn kills it with a shotgun blast to

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:12.950
the face.

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:16.910
This leads us to the very final moment of
the movie where Evelyn and Regan realise what

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:18.169
they have to do.

00:04:18.169 --> 00:04:22.800
As the remaining aliens come running to the
farmhouse attracted by the noise of the gun,

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:26.830
Regan and Evelyn have the hearing aid, speaker
and shotgun at the ready.

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:31.439
According to Lee's white board there should
be two creatures left in the area, so it should

00:04:31.439 --> 00:04:34.080
be possible for them to take them both out.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:38.630
The wider world might also recover if the
discovery can be relayed to others so that

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:42.460
sound-based weapons can be developed to take
down the alien invasion.

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:47.110
By the way, the idea of being pregnant during
this apocalyptic time is interesting both

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:49.460
in terms of the plot and for what it symbolises.

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:54.509
Obviously, it creates a huge problem as not
only is giving birth in total silence impossible,

00:04:54.509 --> 00:04:57.759
but a new-born baby will also naturally cry
out.

00:04:57.759 --> 00:05:02.880
To cope with this, the family builds a special
basement area with a box for the baby complete

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:04.409
with an oxygen tank.

00:05:04.409 --> 00:05:08.569
The underground room is covered with a mattress
which seems to muffle sounds coming from below

00:05:08.569 --> 00:05:11.370
enough to keep any creatures from detecting
them.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:15.430
The birth was actually supposed to take place
in this room but, of course, Evelyn was forced

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:20.210
to give birth in the bathroom while she was
hiding from the alien invading the house.

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:24.650
Symbolically, Evelyn's pregnancy and birth
signals hope for their family and the future

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:29.430
of the world and you can also see this in
the fact that, despite their terrible situation,

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:34.409
Evelyn tries to move forward by home-schooling
her children and both parents try to maintain

00:05:34.409 --> 00:05:37.430
their spirits with family dinners and board
games.

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:42.639
This indicates that the Abbot family is trying
to thrive, not just survive, during this nightmarish

00:05:42.639 --> 00:05:43.860
time.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:47.800
By the way, the scene where Evelyn is in the
flooded basement with the baby is an interesting

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:51.930
call-back to earlier in the film where Lee
showed his son Marcus how the sound of the

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:54.059
waterfall would mask noises they made.

00:05:54.059 --> 00:05:58.400
The sound of the water in the flooding basement
muffled some of the sound of the whimpering

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:03.081
baby, but Evelyn took herself and the baby
behind a sheet of falling water as the baby

00:06:03.081 --> 00:06:07.590
started to cry and just like with the waterfall,
the noise of the falling water was enough

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:09.719
to drown out the baby's crying.

00:06:09.719 --> 00:06:14.430
So, did you enjoy A Quiet Place and what did
you think about the creatures?

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:19.150
Also, would you like to see follow-up stories
set in this universe, along the lines of the

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:20.660
Cloverfield movies?

